{"description":"M0 — the entry point becomes a generated, drift-checked artifact of the repository's own knowledge, not a static paragraph. Today eka-cli/AGENTS.md is a three-line marker stub (f95b87c) and the block generated by bootstrap/agentsmd.go is fixed prose, so the file an agent actually starts from names no constraint and cannot go stale loudly. Build one generator whose input is the repository's committed snapshot (exchange/snapshots/units): identity, the stratum 1-2 constraint index (Discovery req/fnd/vis/str plus Architecture adr/dec/spec/std), bounded and index-only, with content still retrieved through eka get / eka context. Add eka agents-md with --write and --check (regenerate and compare bytes; exit 1 on drift, 2 on usage), reporting the diff summary, plus a --json report. Source the snapshot rather than the workspace store so the check is environment-independent: the committed bytes are the same on a laptop and in CI, and two developers cannot disagree about a committed file. Derive nothing volatile (the active container stays a pointer to eka status) so the file does not churn on every transition. Apply it to eka-cli itself, whose own repository is the failing case, and update the block-budget assertion from a line count to a byte budget, with the rendering decision and the measured token cost recorded.","acceptanceCriteria":"- eka agents-md --check regenerates the block and exits 0 only when the committed region is byte-identical, 1 on drift with the diff summary, 2 on usage or IO error.\n- The generated block names identity, the stratum 1-2 constraint index from the committed snapshot, and the retrieval pointer; it carries no volatile execution state.\n- Block size stays within a declared byte budget (target \u003c= 3200 bytes, roughly 800 tokens), asserted by a test; the existing prose assertions still pass.\n- eka-cli's own AGENTS.md is regenerated and eka agents-md --check exits 0 on it (the primary exit criterion: the repository that ships this must satisfy it).\n- A test proves non-vacuity: perturbing one constraint line in the committed region makes --check exit 1.\n- Only the snapshot reader is authoritative; with no snapshot present the block degrades to identity only and the command says so rather than inventing a list."}